{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the three parameter prior sampling statements so that `a`, `b`, and `sigma` are each given their built-in prior before they are used in the likelihood for `y`. This preserves the original log density because Stan sampling statements add commutative log-density terms. No data changes were required; `N` and `x` remain context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real a;
  real b;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  a ~ normal(0, 10);
  b ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 10);
  y ~ normal(a * exp(-b * x), sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"x":[5.459627033620195,4.34795385027026,4.876193221239422,3.28924278066246],"y":[4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
